  "statement": "Let \\(f(x)=|x-2|+|x-4|\\) \\(-|2x-6|,\\) for \\(2\\le x\\le8.\\) The sum of the largest and smallest values of \\(f(x)\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "On \\([2,3],\\) \\(f(x)=2x-4;\\) on \\([3,4],\\) \\(f(x)=8-2x;\\) and on \\([4,8],\\) \\(f(x)=0.\\) Thus the minimum is \\(0\\) and the maximum is \\(2,\\) whose sum is \\(2.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Break the interval at the zeros \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) and \\(4\\)",
        "Simplify \\(f(x)\\) on each resulting interval"
      ],
